# Vendored kernel UAPI headers (Phase 13)

These are unmodified copies of the DRM userspace API headers from this
repository's own kernel tree (`kernel/include/uapi/drm/`):

    drm.h, drm_mode.h, drm_fourcc.h   (GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note)

Vendoring keeps the userspace build self-contained: Ubuntu does not ship
`linux/drm.h` in `linux-libc-dev`, and libdrm's public headers expose the
libdrm API rather than the raw ioctl structs we drive directly.

Adjustments made to the copies:

    - `#include <linux/bits.h>` and `#include <linux/const.h>` removed from
      drm_mode.h/drm.h/drm_fourcc.h.  Those are kernel-internal headers that
      glibc does not provide, and `BIT()`/`UL()` are not used anywhere in
      these three files.

Nothing else was changed, so ioctl numbers and struct layouts match the
kernel exactly.  `src/bgfx.c` includes them by relative path
(`"uapi/drm/drm.h"`) so no `-I` flag is required anywhere in the build.
